{"name":"Aggressive Aqua","hex":"#00fbff","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aggressive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by aggression; highly combative; prone to behave in a way that involves attacking (especially if unjustly) or arguing.","Tends to attack the player while unprovoked."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who is aggressive.","A (Black) woman who presents as masculine; a butch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aggressive"},{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aggression","blocks":[{"text":"Aggression is behavior aimed at opposing or attacking something or someone. Though often done with the intent to cause harm, some might channel it into creative and practical outlets. It may occur either reactively or without provocation. In humans, aggression can be caused by various triggers. For example, aggression may result from built-up frustration due to blocked goals or perceived disrespect. Human aggression can be classified into direct and indirect aggression; while the former is characterized by physical or verbal behavior intended to cause harm to someone, the latter is characterized by behavior intended to harm the social relations of an individual or group."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Agression_contre_Falli%C3%A8res_-_d%C3%A9tail_%28Petit_Parisien_illustr%C3%A9%2C_1909-01-10%29.jpeg/330px-Agression_contre_Falli%C3%A8res_-_d%C3%A9tail_%28Petit_Parisien_illustr%C3%A9%2C_1909-01-10%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aggression"},{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg/500px-Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg/500px-Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Many mammals, such as the tiger, bare their teeth as a sign of aggression—a form of aposematism. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Elephant_seal_fight_Part-1.jpg/500px-Elephant_seal_fight_Part-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Elephant_se